opam-version: "2.0"
synopsis: "Bech32 and Bech32m for web3 address encodings"
description: """
BIP-173 Bech32 and BIP-350 Bech32m, without the full web3-codec dependency
closure. Depends on nothing: the checksum is integer arithmetic and the
charset is a string, so this links into a MirageOS/Solo5 unikernel and needs
no bignum.

The 90-character cap is BIP-173's and remains the default, but it is a
parameter rather than a constant -- the Cosmos SDK spells addresses in Bech32
and does not enforce it."""
